  [4] USAF National Museum, "Pratt & Whitney F100-PW-220" fact sheet
      https://www.nationalmuseum.af.mil/Visit/Museum-Exhibits/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/196437/pratt-whitney-f100-pw-220/

  [5] Smithsonian NASM, "Pratt & Whitney F100-PW-100 Turbofan Engine"
      https://airandspace.si.edu/collection-objects/pratt-whitney-f100-pw-100-turbofan-engine/nasm_A19900276000

  [6] Purdue University, "F100 Engine Family" specifications
      https://engineering.purdue.edu/~propulsi/propulsion/jets/tfans/f100.html

  [7] Prisacariu & Ciubotaru, "Aspect Regarding of the Pratt & Whitney F100
      Jet Engine Performances," AFASES 2017
      DOI: 10.19062/2247-3173.2017.19.1.20

  [8] JSBSim FGTurbine.cpp thrust calculation source code
      https://github.com/JSBSim-Team/jsbsim/blob/master/src/models/propulsion/FGTurbine.cpp

  [9] NASA TM-104326, "Flight and Static Exhaust Flow Properties of an
